{%- comment -%}
  Edition I — Bureau Nine-style horizontal exhibition. Vertical scroll drives horizontal movement
  through five pre-launch editorial studies; House Principles (Rarity/Precision/Ritual/Longevity,
  sections/caviera-house-codes.liquid) is a completely separate, independent experience — this
  section never reads or writes anything from that system, and never reuses its names.

  CAVIERA is Edition-based, not a permanent catalogue — no product grid, no prices, no Add to Bag.
  Edition I's real 10-12 creations don't exist yet, so this shows five editorial STUDIES (Form /
  Light / Material / The Seal / Edition I) that communicate the future Edition world without
  pretending products are available. #edition-i (the menu's landing target) is unchanged, on this
  same outer <section>, exactly as before.

  ARCHITECTURE (progressive enhancement — the SAME DOM works in both modes, only CSS/JS behaviour
  differs):
    < 1024px, no-JS, or prefers-reduced-motion: .caviera-edition-teaser__track is a plain vertical
      stack in normal document flow — intro, then all five studies, full width, no horizontal
      movement, no sticky viewport. Complete and readable on its own.
    >= 1024px with motion allowed: assets/caviera-edition-exhibition.js turns
      .caviera-edition-teaser__wrapper into a tall vertical scroll distance (measured from the
      track's actual rendered width, not a guessed number — see the JS for the exact calculation),
      .caviera-edition-teaser__viewport becomes position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100svh; overflow:
      hidden, and .caviera-edition-teaser__track receives transform: translate3d(x, 0, 0) mapped
      directly from vertical scroll progress — normal page scroll is the only input; nothing here
      intercepts the wheel or prevents default scrolling. This is an entirely separate system from
      the hero/House Principles' own progress variables (--edition-exhibition-progress here, never
      --caviera-progress or --house-code-progress).

  Theme Editor settings preserved from the previous build: edition_number/edition_status/heading/
  year_label/body/structure_line (same IDs, same defaults) — "01 / Upcoming", "EDITION I", "2026",
  the supporting line, and the optional planned-structure line. The old three-image "media 01/02/03"
  choreography settings are retired (that vertical system no longer exists) in favour of five
  Study image/copy settings below, one per exhibition study.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign study_1_img = section.settings.study_1_image
  assign study_2_img = section.settings.study_2_image
  assign study_3_img = section.settings.study_3_image
  assign study_4_img = section.settings.study_4_image
  assign study_5_img = section.settings.study_5_image
  assign bundled_file = '15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png'

  assign has_meta = false
  if section.settings.edition_number != blank or section.settings.edition_status != blank
    assign has_meta = true
  endif

  # Each study falls back to the SAME bundled photograph when no dedicated image is set, but never
  # visibly repeats it identically — data-derived="true" marks exactly this case so
  # assets/caviera-edition-exhibition.css can apply a distinct static crop per study (see that
  # file). A merchant's own dedicated image never carries this attribute and renders untouched.
  assign study_1_derived = false
  if study_1_img == blank
    assign study_1_derived = true
  endif
  assign study_2_derived = false
  if study_2_img == blank
    assign study_2_derived = true
  endif
  assign study_3_derived = false
  if study_3_img == blank
    assign study_3_derived = true
  endif
  assign study_5_derived = false
  if study_5_img == blank
    assign study_5_derived = true
  endif
-%}
<section id="edition-i" class="caviera-edition-teaser" data-scheme="obsidian">
  <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__wrapper" data-caviera-edition-exhibition>
    <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__viewport">
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__track">

        {%- comment -%} INTRO — the same architectural typography as before, now living as the first item on the horizontal canvas. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__intro">
          {%- if has_meta -%}
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__meta label">
              {{- section.settings.edition_number -}}
              {%- if section.settings.edition_number != blank and section.settings.edition_status != blank %} / {% endif -%}
              {{- section.settings.edition_status -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="caviera-edition-teaser__heading">
              {{ section.settings.heading }}
              {%- if section.settings.year_label != blank -%}
                <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__year">{{ section.settings.year_label }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
            <p class="body-text caviera-edition-teaser__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.structure_line != blank -%}
            <p class="caviera-edition-teaser__structure label">{{ section.settings.structure_line }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__cue" data-caviera-edition-cue aria-hidden="true">The Edition &rarr;</span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} 01 FORM — jewellery silhouette, proportion, geometry. {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="caviera-edition-teaser__study" data-study-index="0" data-study-size="small" data-derived="{{ study_1_derived }}">
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-media">
            {%- if study_1_img != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ study_1_img | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                srcset="{{ study_1_img | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ study_1_img | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
                sizes="30vw"
                width="{{ study_1_img.width }}" height="{{ study_1_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ study_1_img.alt | default: 'Form' | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="Form" loading="lazy">
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-label">
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-index">01 / Form</span>
            {%- if section.settings.study_1_copy != blank -%}<p>{{ section.settings.study_1_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>

        {%- comment -%} 02 LIGHT — diamond, reflection, macro stone, brilliance. {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="caviera-edition-teaser__study" data-study-index="1" data-study-size="medium" data-derived="{{ study_2_derived }}">
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-media">
            {%- if study_2_img != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ study_2_img | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                srcset="{{ study_2_img | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ study_2_img | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
                sizes="36vw"
                width="{{ study_2_img.width }}" height="{{ study_2_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ study_2_img.alt | default: 'Light' | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="Light" loading="lazy">
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-label">
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-index">02 / Light</span>
            {%- if section.settings.study_2_copy != blank -%}<p>{{ section.settings.study_2_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>

        {%- comment -%} 03 MATERIAL — the large hero visual of the sequence: gold, surface, setting. {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="caviera-edition-teaser__study" data-study-index="2" data-study-size="large" data-derived="{{ study_3_derived }}">
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-media">
            {%- if study_3_img != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ study_3_img | image_url: width: 1800 }}"
                srcset="{{ study_3_img | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ study_3_img | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w"
                sizes="48vw"
                width="{{ study_3_img.width }}" height="{{ study_3_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ study_3_img.alt | default: 'Material' | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="Material" loading="lazy">
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-label">
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-index">03 / Material</span>
            {%- if section.settings.study_3_copy != blank -%}<p>{{ section.settings.study_3_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>

        {%- comment -%}
          04 THE SEAL — a formal maker's-mark study, not a fake engraving macro. Uses the real House
          Seal artwork on a plain Obsidian/Cinnabar card unless a merchant has uploaded a genuine
          Seal-engraving photograph. Never the Living Oryx — that mark has no formal-authentication
          role in this theme.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="caviera-edition-teaser__study" data-study-index="3" data-study-size="narrow">
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-media">
            {%- if study_4_img != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ study_4_img | image_url: width: 1000 }}"
                srcset="{{ study_4_img | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ study_4_img | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w"
                sizes="22vw"
                width="{{ study_4_img.width }}" height="{{ study_4_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ study_4_img.alt | default: 'The Seal' | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__seal-card" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: 'dark', width: 96, alt: '' -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-label">
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-index">04 / The Seal</span>
            {%- if section.settings.study_4_copy != blank -%}<p>{{ section.settings.study_4_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>

        {%- comment -%} 05 EDITION I — the exhibition's final pre-launch state; resolves before Object in focus enters. {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="caviera-edition-teaser__study" data-study-index="4" data-study-size="medium" data-derived="{{ study_5_derived }}">
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-media">
            {%- if study_5_img != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ study_5_img | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                srcset="{{ study_5_img | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ study_5_img | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
                sizes="36vw"
                width="{{ study_5_img.width }}" height="{{ study_5_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ study_5_img.alt | default: 'Edition I' | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="Edition I" loading="lazy">
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-label">
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__study-index">05 / Edition I</span>
            {%- if section.settings.study_5_copy != blank -%}<p>{{ section.settings.study_5_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'caviera-edition-exhibition.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Edition I",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_number", "label": "Number", "default": "01" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_status", "label": "Status", "default": "Upcoming", "info": "Quiet metadata, not a sale badge — avoid hype language (\"Limited drop\", \"Only X left\", \"Coming soon!!!\")." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "EDITION I" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "year_label", "label": "Year", "default": "2026" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "The first CAVIERA Edition is in preparation." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "structure_line", "label": "Structure line (optional)", "info": "e.g. \"10–12 creations\" — only if clearly framed as the planned Edition structure, never current inventory. Leave blank if the composition is stronger without it." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "01 Form" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "study_1_image", "label": "Form image", "info": "Jewellery silhouette, proportion, geometry. Falls back to a bundled CAVIERA photograph when left blank." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "study_1_copy", "label": "Short line", "default": "Proportion before ornament." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "02 Light" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "study_2_image", "label": "Light image", "info": "Diamond, reflection, macro stone, brilliance. Falls back to the same bundled photograph (differently cropped) when left blank." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "study_2_copy", "label": "Short line", "default": "Light held with precision." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "03 Material" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "study_3_image", "label": "Material image", "info": "Gold, surface, edge, setting detail. Falls back to the same bundled photograph (differently cropped) when left blank." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "study_3_copy", "label": "Short line", "default": "Material, resolved with intent." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "04 The Seal" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "study_4_image", "label": "The Seal image (optional)", "info": "Only if a genuine House Seal engraving/authentication photograph exists. Falls back to a formal card using the official House Seal artwork when left blank." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "study_4_copy", "label": "Short line", "default": "The House leaves its mark." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "05 Edition I" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "study_5_image", "label": "Edition I image (optional)", "info": "A final, distinct cinematic crop. Falls back to the same bundled photograph (differently cropped) when left blank." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "study_5_copy", "label": "Short line (optional)" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Edition I" }],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["index"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
